    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "I'd like to auto-insert semicolons in Nix code, e.g. when the code is like\r\n\r\n```nix\r\n{\r\n  some_thing = \r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nwhen I type a `{` at the end of the line, I'd like it to expand to the following, where `|` is my cursor position.\r\n\r\n```nix\r\n{\r\n  some_thing = { | };\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI tried this in a `ftplugin` for Nix, but this puts my cursor between the `}` and the `;` instead of between `{}`:\r\n\r\n```nix\r\nlocal mp = require('mini.pairs')\r\n\r\nmp.map_buf(0, 'i', '{', { action = 'open', pair = '{};', register = { cr = false } })\r\nmp.map_buf(0, 'i', '}', { action = 'close', pair = '{};', register = { cr = false } })\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf possible, I'd also like to _not_ insert the semicolon if the `{}` is inside a list type, like\r\n\r\n```nix\r\n{\r\n  things = [\r\n    # since this is inside square brackets, don't add the ;\r\n    { }\r\n  ];\r\n}\r\n```",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I'd like to auto-insert semicolons in Nix code, e.g. when the code is like</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-nix notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"{\n  some_thing = \n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n  some_thing <span class=\"pl-kos\">=</span> \n<span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">when I type a <code class=\"notranslate\">{</code> at the end of the line, I'd like it to expand to the following, where <code class=\"notranslate\">|</code> is my cursor position.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-nix notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"{\n  some_thing = { | };\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-c1\">some_thing</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span> | <span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I tried this in a <code class=\"notranslate\">ftplugin</code> for Nix, but this puts my cursor between the <code class=\"notranslate\">}</code> and the <code class=\"notranslate\">;</code> instead of between <code class=\"notranslate\">{}</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-nix notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"local mp = require('mini.pairs')\n\nmp.map_buf(0, 'i', '{', { action = 'open', pair = '{};', register = { cr = false } })\nmp.map_buf(0, 'i', '}', { action = 'close', pair = '{};', register = { cr = false } })\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-en\"><span class=\"pl-s1\">local</span></span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">mp</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">require</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span>'<span class=\"pl-s1\">mini</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">pairs'</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-s1\">mp</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">map_buf</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">0</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> '<span class=\"pl-s1\">i'</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> '<span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>'<span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">action</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">=</span> '<span class=\"pl-s1\">open'</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-en\"><span class=\"pl-s1\">pair</span></span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">=</span> '<span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>'<span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> register <span class=\"pl-kos\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span> cr <span class=\"pl-kos\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">false</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span>\n<span class=\"pl-s1\">mp</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">map_buf</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">0</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> '<span class=\"pl-s1\">i'</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> '<span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span>'<span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">action</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">=</span> '<span class=\"pl-s1\">close'</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-en\"><span class=\"pl-s1\">pair</span></span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">=</span> '<span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>'<span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> register <span class=\"pl-kos\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span> cr <span class=\"pl-kos\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">false</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If possible, I'd also like to <em>not</em> insert the semicolon if the <code class=\"notranslate\">{}</code> is inside a list type, like</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-nix notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"{\n  things = [\n    # since this is inside square brackets, don't add the ;\n    { }\n  ];\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-c1\">things</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">[</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-c\"># since this is inside square brackets, don't add the ;</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-kos\">]</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span></pre></div>",
    "bodyText": "I'd like to auto-insert semicolons in Nix code, e.g. when the code is like\n{\n  some_thing = \n}\nwhen I type a { at the end of the line, I'd like it to expand to the following, where | is my cursor position.\n{\n  some_thing = { | };\n}\nI tried this in a ftplugin for Nix, but this puts my cursor between the } and the ; instead of between {}:\nlocal mp = require('mini.pairs')\n\nmp.map_buf(0, 'i', '{', { action = 'open', pair = '{};', register = { cr = false } })\nmp.map_buf(0, 'i', '}', { action = 'close', pair = '{};', register = { cr = false } })\nIf possible, I'd also like to not insert the semicolon if the {} is inside a list type, like\n{\n  things = [\n    # since this is inside square brackets, don't add the ;\n    { }\n  ];\n}",
